WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.399
Week ten.

00:00:01.449 --> 00:00:05.520
Inside the world of influencer marketing, with Bryce Coombe from Hypetap.

00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:07.489
Australians spend twenty nine and a half hours a month on TikTok.

00:00:07.539 --> 00:00:12.573
And eighty percent are there mainly for creator content.

00:00:13.167 --> 00:00:16.543
Seventy five percent have acted on something they saw in their feed.

00:00:16.593 --> 00:00:18.251
And social is now search:

00:00:18.301 --> 00:00:21.743
nearly half of US consumers use TikTok as a search engine.

00:00:22.333 --> 00:00:24.459
A creator showing the product in real life,

00:00:24.509 --> 00:00:25.386
like a recipe,

00:00:25.436 --> 00:00:26.758
gets positive sentiment.

00:00:26.808 --> 00:00:29.517
Strict brand scripts get neutral at best.

00:00:30.133 --> 00:00:32.829
And the brand is liable, not the influencer.

00:00:32.879 --> 00:00:35.630
A free product counts as paid, so disclose it.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:37.917
And never trust a screen grab.

00:00:38.533 --> 00:00:41.764
Views and engagement explain attention, not growth.

00:00:41.814 --> 00:00:46.653
Measure mental availability, share of voice, perception, and behaviour change.

00:00:47.267 --> 00:00:48.880
Know your brand's eye level.

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:51.000
A leader brand uses experts.

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.009
An eye to eye brand uses creators who are just like you.

00:00:53.059 --> 00:00:56.899
A subservient brand does the work for people.

00:00:57.500 --> 00:00:58.577
The takeaway?

00:00:58.627 --> 00:01:02.380
Treat influencer as a specialist discipline, and measure growth.
